+# Twice-padded width-fifteen witness: exact filtered lift scan
+
+## Outcome
+
+All **1,987,440** admissible symmetric, center-even completions of the
+120 surviving four-coordinate prefixes were checked. None shared eight
+complete actual carry words at observations `t=0,...,7`.
+
+The initial ordered difference was exactly
+
+```text
+[0,0,1,-3,5,-6,6,-6,6,-6,5,-3,1,0,0].
+```
+
+Swapping the ordered words covers the negative sign. The width is exactly
+fifteen. No arbitrary-width exclusion or global memory sharpness is claimed.
+
+The exact survivor counts are conditional on the eight-observation prefix
+filter already having been applied:
+
+| Number of complete actual carry words additionally matched | Surviving word pairs |
+|---:|---:|
+| 0 | 1,987,440 |
+| 1 | 172,200 |
+| 2 | 62,784 |
+| 3 | 49,776 |
+| 4 | 27,370 |
+| 5 | 15,024 |
+| 6 | 4,910 |
+| 7 | 126 |
+| 8 | 0 |
+
+The scan completed with exit code zero. Its measured wall time was
+0.4603 seconds, with a child peak of 10,240 KiB under this invocation.
+
+## Exhaustive domain and filter boundary
+
+The full admissible ordered domain has
+
+`18 * 19 * 18 * 16 * 14 * 13 * 13 * 7 = 1,631,290,752`
+
+word pairs. The first four coordinates have 98,496 possibilities, with
+oriented difference `(0,0,1,-3)`. The supplied exact four-prefix computation
+retains 120 of them after eight abstract observations.
+
+For each retained right-hand prefix, the scan enumerates every choice
+
+```text
+r4 = 0..13,
+r5 = 6..18,
+r6 = 0..12,
+r7 in {6,8,10,12,14,16,18}.
+```
+
+Each choice is reflected to obtain the complete symmetric word; the left
+word is the right word plus the prescribed difference. Thus every retained
+prefix has exactly `14 * 13 * 13 * 7 = 16,562` completions. Assertions check
+the count separately for each prefix, all coefficient ranges, symmetry,
+nonzero exterior coefficient, and center parity.
+
+The prefix graph uses one shared incoming bit at `L-4` and requires all
+four low carries and all four reflected high carries—including the terminal
+carry—to agree at each observation. The CSV contains only the first
+compatible bit string as metadata. **That string is not used to restrict
+the actual lift scan.** Each complete candidate follows its own actual
+carry trajectory.
+
+The four-prefix source, CSV, result, and verification receipt are copied
+unchanged from the scout's `agent10-count/four-prefix-check-002` directory.
+Their hashes were checked before the lift scan. The original source
+enumerates every shared bit path, cross-checks its digit and arithmetic
+updates, and validates its three-prefix mode against the previously checked
+control counts.
+
+The four-prefix actual-history inclusion has **not been formalized in
+Lean**. Consequently, the directly checked statement is the absence of
+eight-word collisions inside all 1,987,440 retained completions. Extending
+that negative conclusion to the full width-fifteen domain uses the
+correctness and completeness of the computational necessary-prefix
+projection. The current Lean three-column inclusion does not by itself
+certify this four-column filter.
+
+## Actual simulator and reproducibility
+
+`actual_simulator.inc` contains the byte-for-byte unchanged `admissible`,
+`carries`, and `next_pairs` functions from the earlier
+`agent10-semantic/padded_witness_scan.cpp`. Carry vectors include index zero
+and the terminal carry. Equality compares the complete vectors, so differing
+widths would also be detected. Each update calculates the actual decimal
+sum digits, appends terminal overflow if present, and forms the next pair
+word from those digits.
+
+Run from this directory:
+
+```bash
+g++ -std=c++17 -O3 -Wall -Wextra -Werror twice_padded_witness_scan.cpp -o twice_padded_witness_scan
+./twice_padded_witness_scan survivors-4.csv first_eight_collision.json > result.json
+python replay_seven_word.py > seven_word_integer_replay.json
+```
+
+No first-eight-collision file is created for the recorded result. The full
+search output is `result.json`; the exact command, source/input hashes,
+exit code, elapsed time, and peak child RSS are in `scan.command.json`.
+The additional receipt `lift_verification.json` hashes the source and all
+retained inputs and outputs.
+
+## Independent ordinary-integer control
+
+One of the 126 seven-word survivors has canonical representatives
+
+```text
+n = 900000058163209
+m = 900000082716109.
+```
+
+Its initial pair words are
+
+```text
+q = [18,0,2,3,6,1,8,10,8,1,6,3,2,0,18]
+r = [18,0,1,6,1,7,2,16,2,7,1,6,1,0,18].
+```
+
+The independent Python replay constructs the ordinary integers, checks
+their exact initial pair words, and repeatedly applies
+`n + int(str(n)[::-1])`. Complete carries agree at times zero through six
+and first differ at time seven. The overflow pattern across the seven
+matching observations is `ONOOONN`.
+
+`seven_word_integer_replay.json` retains all decimal integers, reversals,
+next integers, decimal digit arrays, pair words, and complete carry arrays
+at times zero through eight. Integer values are stored as strings to
+preserve exactness in JSON consumers with fixed-precision numeric types.
+`replay_seven_word.py` reproduces the trace.
+
+This positive example is independently replayed computational evidence;
+its existence does not depend on completeness of the negative-search
+filter. No new Lean certificate or optimal universal observation bound is
+claimed here.
